From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: A shortcut whose program is gone asks to delete it (5966)

Zoom Workplace's uninstaller (an MSI whose custom action makes the
shortcut and nothing removes it) left its Public desktop shortcut;
double-clicking it said "Path not found." Windows asks instead: the item
the shortcut opens has been moved or removed -- delete the shortcut?

- ShellLink_InvokeCommand: a target on a fixed local disk that is not
  there asks "Problem with Shortcut"; Yes puts the shortcut in the Recycle
  Bin (SHFileOperation, which asks an administrator's consent for one
  everyone shares). With CMIC_MASK_FLAG_NO_UI nothing is shown and the
  open fails with ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND.
- A shortcut's handler that ran and stopped (that question, or its
  target's ShellExecuteEx failing, which said why) ends the open:
  ShellExecute_FromContextMenu stops on ERROR_CANCELLED from a handler
  and SHELL_execute returns FALSE with the handler's error. It went on to
  treat the .lnk itself as the file -- after 5965 an Open with for the
  shortcut came up after "Path not found.". Open with is never offered
  for a .lnk or .url.
- do_error_dialog keeps the caller's last error past its message box.

Gate test-deadlink (dead shortcut Yes/No/no-UI, a working one, an
unstartable target), mutants SG_MUTANT_DEAD_LINK_ERROR and
SG_MUTANT_LINK_FALLTHROUGH.
